[size=5][b]Blender to the native Rust client — custom asset experiments[/b][/size]

AI-assisted Blender authoring and native-format conversion for original RuneScape-inspired assets. Images distinguish Blender renders, native previews and live placements.

[b]Blender-to-native conversion[/b]

The first procedural arch was exported from Blender, converted to the native model format and placed in an isolated live world. Blender lighting and materials do not transfer unchanged.

[SPOILER=Blender conversion and first live placement]

[i]Blender render — The first procedural Cinderworks arch, shown in Blender studio lighting.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/custom-models/01-first-blender.png[/img]

[i]Prepared native render — The same original arch after conversion, through the native software renderer.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/custom-models/02-first-native.png[/img]

[i]Live native gameplay — The original arch placed in an isolated live Rust client/server test.[/i]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/autismoyah-hub/project-gielinor-showcase/83e1b40d52b34bcbe50b5d9662f5a61a37bb2282/images/custom-models/03-first-live.png[/img]

[/SPOILER]

[b]Reference checks and original machinery[/b]

The anvil compares an authentic reference with an independently modeled reconstruction. The riveting station and screw press are original designs. Export success and silhouette scores do not establish artistic quality.

[SPOILER=Anvil reference and original machinery]

[i]Prepared native comparison — Authentic Jagex anvil on the left; independently authored reconstruction on the right. Same native camera and light.[/i]
